# Munim T3 Connect client identifiers — install as ~/.mt/munim-connect.env
# (also mirrored to Windows build hosts as %USERPROFILE%\.mt\munim-connect.env
# by scripts/personal-refresh-windows.sh).
#
# While ~/.mt/munim-connect.env does not exist, every build behaves exactly as
# today. Once it exists with the three required values, the hosted web deploy
# (scripts/personal-publish-web.sh) and the desktop fleet builds
# (scripts/personal-refresh-mac.sh / personal-refresh-win.ps1 /
# personal-publish-munim-win.ps1 / personal-publish-github-release.sh) bake
# Munim's own Connect configuration instead of T3's.
#
# PUBLIC IDENTIFIERS ONLY. Never put CLERK_SECRET_KEY here — relay-side
# secrets belong in ~/.mt/munim-relay.env (see personal-munim-relay.env.example).

# Clerk Dashboard > (MT Code app) > API keys > Publishable key.
T3CODE_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_live_...

# Name of the JWT template created in Clerk Dashboard > JWT templates.
# Template claims must be { "aud": "t3-code-relay" }.
T3CODE_CLERK_JWT_TEMPLATE=t3-relay

# Optional Munim relay URL. Omit to reach computers through pairing / Computer
# Use (no paid relay stack).
# T3CODE_RELAY_URL=https://mtcode-relay.munimtech.com

# Optional until the CLI OAuth application exists (Clerk Dashboard > OAuth
# applications > public client with PKCE; scopes openid, profile, email;
# redirect URIs http://127.0.0.1:34338/callback and a /connect/callback on
# whatever origin serves the Connect page). Without it, `t3 connect`
# reports missing configuration; web/desktop sign-in still works.
# T3CODE_CLERK_CLI_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=...

# Both `t3 connect` OAuth flows start at a hosted app's /connect page, which
# defaults to https://app.t3.codes (T3's deployment, wrong Clerk instance for
# Munim builds). MT Code no longer publishes a hosted app of its own, so set
# this only if you stand one up. Runtime-read by the server, and exported at
# build time alongside the values above.
# T3CODE_HOSTED_APP_URL=https://mt.example.test
